# Canonical identities.
#
# git log, shortlog, blame and `git log --author` all read this file, so an old
# handle displays as the current one everywhere without rewriting history. The
# alternative — rebasing to change author fields — would give 284 of main's 299
# commits new SHAs, orphan 29 remote branches and break every existing clone,
# to fix something that is presentation.
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email>  Old Name <old@email>

Dee <dee@autonomous.ai>  brody <brody@autonomous.ai>
Dee <dee@autonomous.ai>  Dee <brody@autonomous.ai>
Dee <dee@autonomous.ai>  dee <dee@autonomous.ai>
